claimed: okay-script-measured -- the numbers okay-script has never had (operator ask 2026-09-07, first of four: measure, then warm+stats, then an image, then a guide). What a page COSTS: the cold first render (dotc in-process, per page shape), the warm re-invoke, the recompile a file change forces, a static file's serve, a 304's, and what a compiled page holds in memory; plus the concurrency the container actually reaches on one Site. Deliberately NOT JMH: every sample here is milliseconds-to-seconds and each fork would recompile the pages, so the harness is a Live-tagged measured run (medians of n, warmup discarded, host load recorded) that PRINTS a table and asserts only sanity bounds, never a threshold that turns a slow CI box into a red build. Adds okay-script/src/test/.../MeasureScript.scala and a docs/benchmarks.md section with the method and the numbers.
